        "id": 150066,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-11-19T20:52:36.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Both MTM and Bot9th work with their real-time elements turned into turn-based style. &nbsp;MTM includes the rules to do it.</p><p>This game would almost need to be a small print game that would have to build traction from in order to get rereleased. &nbsp;But that kind of time and investment with little return isn't feasible for a company GtG's size.</p><p>I do find it surprising that New Bedford could get 100k and Monster truck Mayhem can't get 25k. &nbsp;I guess whaling doesn't put off people as much as real time dice do.</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:28:39.164Z",
